<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Adaptive icon foreground: the amber folder with a double-headed transfer arrow.

     The art sits inside the central 72x72 safe zone (x and y from 18 to 90), because a
     launcher may crop anything outside it.

     Folder and arrow are one path with android:fillType="evenOdd", so the arrow is a real
     hole rather than a shape painted in the background colour. That matters because the
     launcher moves the foreground and background independently when you tilt the device —
     a fake knockout would visibly slide out of register. It also means the monochrome
     (themed icon) layer works: Android recolours the folder and the hole stays a hole. -->
